+++ b/docs/research/sfcc-arrangement-a/caller-checklist.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# Candidate A connected callers
+
+- `pipeline::run_sfcc_pipeline_impl`: existing octree/classification remains; activated construction uses actual final represented domains. All native strategies receive real disjoint cell groups; separate point pools merge with exact witnesses. Derived feature graph is retained through normal assembly and final audits.
+- `worker::prepare`, resumable preparation and `decide_partition`: unchanged classifier and original prepared fingerprint. The construction does not increase default depth or alter prepared decisions.
+- `worker::mesh_partition`: original preparation fingerprint checked before construction; activated workers emit only their Morton group. Failed activated requests retain explicit local uncertainty.
+- `worker::merge_partials`: SFP6 decoding, field/lattice/family checks, fresh complete geometry/feature construction and exact receiver comparison. `merge` recovery policy stays unchanged; mandatory coarse fallback succeeds without recovery.
+- `local_coverage`: construction-family report, exact original signed-box field signature, imported failure records, fresh receiver snapshots, existing cleanup proof lifecycle.
+- `PointTable`: one per-export family flag; existing global keys, six-field snapshots, protected curve intervals, patch owners, compaction and float32 export remain.
+- `assembly::finish`: unchanged. Existing debris cleanup, protected edges, checked flips and optional quality editing all run.
+- `feature_set`: fresh run-ID allocator exposed internally for the derived graph; legacy feature compiler unchanged.
+- `src/export/export.mts`: optional localCoverage.scope string union includes signedBoxArrangement.
+- Historical documentation/evidence is not edited. Obstruction desired assertions change only after both independent exact geometry oracles pass the actual production mesh.
