+# Candidate A: finite signed-box arrangement construction
+
+This candidate starts at `04d889f911ba6c89981752df02cc2ad7a67ddc0f`. It adds a bounded construction rather than interpreting the prior necessary edge guard as a meshing theorem. This report describes candidate code, not a consensus decision.
+
+## Target and supported domain
+
+The target is the complete zero set of the continuous real hard Min/Max expression induced by the actual stored binary64 coefficients. Every leaf must be a box with actual identity transform, scale one, zero transform translation, finite center, finite positive half extents, and sign exactly +1 or -1. Each represented `center ± half` must equal its exact dyadic sum. Nonempty Min/Max nodes and every original occurrence/path are retained. An advisory leaf ID is never an identity. No smooth blend, rotation, nonidentity similarity, generic distance sampling, or relaxed zero sign enters this theorem.
+
+The production fallback is activated only if the prepared octree still contains a degenerate cell, and the complete target arrangement finds two distinct parallel exposed planes in at least one represented cell. This is a conservative use of existing unresolved discovery/refinement state. It is not a proof that all possible legacy mesher failures trigger fallback. Healthy octrees do not receive a full arrangement preflight. The standalone constructor tests more targets than this deliberately narrow activation rule.
+
+The constructor checks lattice depth/resolution/span/step before integer shifts and packing; validates each actual cell key and index; and requires `cell_aabb` endpoints equal the shared `point_to_world` endpoints. It uses those actual rounded finite domains. It does not claim they equal an ideal unrounded real affine lattice. All exposed rectangles must lie in exactly one actual closed leaf domain. Any original primitive endpoint plane coincident with any represented leaf boundary coordinate is explicitly outside this construction (`GridContact`), including lower-dimensional tangencies to otherwise empty closed cells; no half-open ownership claim is made. Overlapping owners and missing surface owners fail. The supplied canonical prepared partition is the normal input premise; the receiver independently checks all represented target facets against its union of represented cells.
+
+## Complete stratum enumeration
+
+Each axis is partitioned by every original box endpoint and every represented leaf boundary inside the union of primitive bounds. The Cartesian product is a conforming common refinement of all leaf interfaces, including 2:1 neighbors. Equal real binary64 values, including +0/-0, share one coordinate rank. Original operand bits and syntax remain in the field signature.
+
+An axis atom is either a coordinate point (even rank) or the open interval between consecutive points (odd rank). A box sign on a product atom is exactly +1 if any axis atom is exterior, 0 if none is exterior and at least one is an endpoint, and -1 otherwise; multiply by the leaf sign. Apply the original Min/Max tree to these integer signs. This computes the sign of the original real field on **every** open 3D, 2D, 1D, and 0D stratum without choosing a rounded midpoint. Consecutive binary64 endpoints therefore remain valid atoms even if no intervening binary64 point exists.
+
+An exposed 2D zero stratum must have strictly opposite signs in its two adjacent open 3D strata. Orient its rectangle toward the positive side. Every other zero stratum must belong to the closure of these exposed rectangles. A zero-only sheet, isolated edge, or isolated point is rejected, rather than regularized away. The complete regular rectangle complex is also checked for opposed edge incidence and connected cyclic vertex links; edge/point contacts between solids fail even when every zero stratum belongs to an exposed closure. The exterior of the union bounding box has a constant signed-tree sign; negative exterior is rejected as an unbounded solid.
+
+For each exposed rectangle, recursively retain every zero leaf whose sign wins along its entire original ancestor path. Duplicate or coincident planes may share the geometric rectangle but keep all active original occurrences. This is an exposure argument, not a sampled winner query. Original source paths can be reconstructed exactly from the signed-tree signature and are retained in the arrangement occurrence manifest.
+
+## Construction and cell-relative correspondence
+
+Every target rectangle receives its two oriented diagonal triangles. The tensor-product coordinate event identities give equal vertices and equal subdivisions on all incident target rectangles. Cuts induced by finer cells extend through the entire relevant arrangement, so an unsplit coarse-side edge cannot meet two fine-side edges. Global key identity is the exact canonical coordinate bit tuple, which is an event identity; there is no proximity welding.
+
+Each rectangle is assigned to its actual owning leaf before emission. Cells can own several disks, patches with holes, a closed component with no face trace, or several closed components. These cases use the same complete 3D/2D/1D/0D enumeration, rather than triangulating observed boundary loops independently. The union of all owned triangles is exactly the independently enumerated target complex. This gives an actual per-cell correspondence, not a proof inferred from whole-output manifold counts.
+
+The complete exposed crease graph is derived from rectangle edges whose two incident rectangles have different normals. Each atomic crease is an existing straight `FeatureCurve` with exact checked endpoints and interval [0,1]. Artificial degree-two nodes subdivide a longer straight crease at shared arrangement cuts; they do not add geometric creases. Each carrier chooses one canonical active original occurrence for the existing quality API, while the full target manifest retains ties. Every required crease is independently enumerated before feature memberships are emitted. The existing nonempty feature-chain audit runs against this graph. Legacy feature compilation remains untouched for healthy exports.
+
+An exploratory probe demonstrates why the legacy graph cannot simply be treated as the new proof graph: four coarse crease segments cross a compiler split at x=-1.4049600000000004, and a later exposed component reuses geometrically coincident plane carriers whose original leaf does not itself vanish there. This is a mismatch with the stronger new exposure contract, not a claim that the legacy carrier API promised all active ownership.
+
+## Float32 and cleanup
+
+Every distinct axis event must map to a distinct finite float32 value in the same strict order. The product of the three increasing piecewise affine coordinate maps is an ambient homeomorphism; it maps every source arrangement rectangle and its diagonal triangles to the exported float32 rectangles/triangles. This prevents sheet collapse, self-intersections, and triangle degeneracy within this construction. Primitive plane locations can move by their float32 rounding error. When the primitive endpoints are themselves exact float32 values, as in the mandatory witness, the exported surface is exactly the original target. In general the coordinate error is bounded by the largest rounding displacement on each axis, and the Euclidean displacement by the norm of those three maxima.
+
+This statement applies to the constructed mesh and unchanged output. The existing assembly/debris/cleanup/quality stages run. Closed oriented components survive the existing debris rule; there is no new bypass. Existing checked coplanar sliver flips transport the cell proof via the already established common-refinement capability. Other quality edits must retain the exact witness or withdraw it. Late withdrawal remains a validation limitation and does not convert completed quality editing into an earlier mesher failure.
+
+## Partition and receiver contract
+
+Serial and native partition strategies use the same complete plan. Separate strategies allocate distinct point tables and emit only each group's owned cells. Real WASM workers independently reconstruct the plan from the same prepared leaf payload, derive the same feature graph, and emit only their assigned group. They do not send a full root mesh disguised as a partial. Worker protocol SFP6 adds an arrangement-family bit; mixed families are rejected.
+
+At reception the original field signature, lattice and derived feature fingerprint must agree. All incoming cell identities are unique. The receiver rebuilds the complete target arrangement over represented cells, reconstructs the expected owned triangles and all six binary64 vertex payload fields, and compares them with actual merged geometry. It checks every curve membership, including empty membership sets, and reconstructs complete lifecycle snapshots. Incoming success bits and optional snapshots are not proofs. A missing facet, misassigned cell triangle, changed key/payload, or additional interval invalidates the witness. Receiver construction is an expected-result verification; the received geometry is retained, never replaced by a master serial regeneration.
+
+## Finite resource bounds
+
+Budgets are checked before tensor allocation: at most 4,096 original tree nodes and depth128; 128 distinct coordinates per axis; 65,536 represented cells; 2,000,000 product strata; 16,384 exposed rectangles; 32,000,000 conservative sign/owner work units; and 8,000,000 rectangle-owner or initial leaf-box visits. Sign work includes original internal nodes and repeated subtree scans in ownership collection: the conservative multiplier is `strata * nodes * (2*maximumOccurrenceDepth+3)`. Coordinate insertion deduplicates under the axis cap before Cartesian expansion. The sign array is linear in the capped stratum count; target rectangles, incidence maps, manifests, and feature metadata are bounded by the rectangle cap. Per-worker expected planning is deliberately duplicated and is not claimed to be an optimized architecture.
+
+A failed required fallback produces explicit per-cell arithmetic, budget, zero-stratum, nonmanifold, grid-contact, cell-ownership or float-collapse uncertainty. Unsupported arithmetic for an otherwise healthy decimal box does not force a new fallback or a false certificate. Cancellation is checked during classification and existing export checkpoints discard cancelled results. State is stack/export owned; no cross-export cache is introduced.
+
+## Discovery history versus final outcome
+
+The new constructor resolves a failed simple-cell meshing premise; it does not retroactively make that premise true. The original prepared leaf payload and each first decision remain unchanged. In the mandatory scene the same 106 prepared leaves still include cells marked degenerate, and responsible coarse regions still ask the discovery rule to split. The complete constructor then supplies every required piece despite the fixed depth ceiling. Its fresh successful local witnesses mark their final outcome resolved, so final mesh statistics report zero degenerate/unresolved cells. Profiling emits the actual `box-arrangement` per-cell geometry and a terminal snapshot of these final witnesses. The preserved WASM evidence includes both the original `targetedCells` decision flags and final successful coverage/geometry.
+
+SFP6 parser reads use checked `u64 -> usize` conversion for lengths and indices. Protected and face-use list counts are bounded by payload length. Tagged leaf level and coordinate indices are validated before any shift or cell-key packing. A real final WASM mutation adds 2^32 to the scope-signature count while preserving its low word and every other valid byte; it is rejected rather than wrapping into a valid count on wasm32.
