+# Candidate A result
+
+Baseline: `04d889f911ba6c89981752df02cc2ad7a67ddc0f`. Candidate runtime logical digest: `701a4b0aecb9fa739f62fe219717bd0172df24dca4de8ac0069427f2f8a51dbd`. The matching final focused WASM is `74a47f6b940d192d9083708657531d004013d86c03711a75eea0ee4f8791a92c`, 1,577,588 bytes. It is archived at `/tmp/sfcc-arrangement-a-artifacts/pkg`; source file hashes and the digest recipe's ordered inputs are in [manifest.json](manifest.json).
+
+The mandatory original coarse scene now constructs both complete cuboid boundaries at the unchanged world cube and default depth: 106 represented leaves, 424 independently exposed rectangles, 848 triangles, two components with Euler characteristic two each, zero unresolved, `ok=true`. The output includes all x=.25,.5,.75 sheets in every responsible region. The old root had 700 triangles, one component and72 unresolved. This is a different, complete geometry result, not a performance comparison with equivalent work.
+
+The constructor is a finite tensor-product arrangement over original box planes and actual prepared-leaf boundary coordinates. It retains signed original paths, classifies every open-dimensional stratum by exact order, rejects zero-only/contact singularities, derives the full exposed crease graph, and verifies exact cell-owned output at worker reception. [Proof and limits](proof.md) and [connected callers](caller-checklist.md) give the precise contract.
+
+## Evidence
+
+Two independent exact checks audit actual output. Candidate A's Fraction oracle verifies disjoint rectangle tiling of all twelve expected target facets and equality of the triangle buffer to that construction. The coordinator's independent triangle oracle verifies exact oriented facet coverage, no overlap, total area400 and signed volume288 on both native and WASM float32 output. Indexed topology is checked separately. Raw data is retained in [coarse-native.json](coarse-native.json), [coarse-arrangement.json](coarse-arrangement.json), and [coarse-wasm.json](coarse-wasm.json).
+
+Actual WASM worker instances at1/2/4/8 partitions preserve canonical oriented all-eight-field triangle geometry, feature intervals and full validation in both completion orders. The coarse case also prepares through actual per-round decision workers at those counts and agrees bytewise with serial preparation. Serial recovery is false. [workers-wasm.json](workers-wasm.json) records the mesh results. Native tests additionally exercise the resumable builder, independent point pools, receiver mutations, two-to-one interfaces, translated grids, wholly enclosed components, disjoint enclosed boxes, thin hollow walls, annular patches, nested signs, operand reordering and duplicated geometry/IDs.
+
+The original single sphere, ordinary box, positive clipped-box seam, fine three-sheet export and quality controls retain their successful established paths. The final activation predicate skips full arrangement enumeration for healthy octrees. It does not promise to detect every legacy mesher failure that lacks a prepared degenerate cell.
+
+## Validation and provenance
+
+Native commands use `/opt/homebrew/bin/cargo`, `RUSTC=/opt/homebrew/bin/rustc` (1.99), offline release, one Cargo job and isolated targets. WASM uses Rust1.96, `wasm-pack --target web`, release defaults and `RUSTFLAGS=-C target-feature=+simd128`; Node is26.11.1. No compiler flags, tolerance, depth, or quality switch was changed.
+
+Final source checks:
+
