+- Serde library:202 passed; arrangement integration12, coverage4, discovery6 passed.
+- Profile library:205 passed; arrangement integration12 and coverage6 passed.
+- Final matching WASM focused gate:12 passed,0 failed/skipped/cancelled (17.57s).
+- Final matching WASM malformed-envelope negative: rejected a 2^32 high-word scope-count mutation as required.
+
+Earlier broad WASM run:36 passed on the integrated constructor before final activation, generic-grid-contact and parser hardening. This is precursor evidence, not mislabeled final-artifact coverage. Subsequent12-fixture runs passed after those geometry changes and before the last leaf-level bounds check. The final focused gate is recorded separately. The coordinator owns the eventual application build and broader final acceptance; this candidate did not run browser/visual QA or `make build`.
+
+Preserved experiments include the initial overly strict annulus fixture assertion: the smaller cube already reconstructed its hole with the legacy path, so expecting arrangement scope was wrong. The actual coarse annulus fixture uses a larger cube at unchanged default depth and requires successful arrangement construction. The earlier precision-negative JSON parser produced an inexact represented endpoint; the corrected direct dyadic fixture reaches the intended float32-collapse rejection. The old compiled-carrier probe is retained as a passing diagnostic of its mismatch with the stronger exposure contract, not as a production dependency.
+
+## Cost and remaining scope
+
+The final WASM grows by90,826 bytes over the accepted Step4 focused artifact (1,486,762 bytes). Storage and work caps are specified in the proof, including original internal-node ownership rescans and Cartesian products before allocation. Planning and verification are duplicated per worker; this is a deliberate bounded correctness design, not an optimized parallel mesher.
+
+The coordinator held other agent builds/tests for the matched final WASM timing campaign. Same Node26.11.1, accepted Step4 baseline package and final candidate; one warmup each then five alternating measured pairs per version. The timer encloses only the complete export call; canonical geometry, all eight vertex fields, exact feature interval bits and full validation are compared outside the timer. [Raw rows](cost.jsonl) retain every sample.
